from (values
('115.38.c.10.A',3,'Which strategy best helps a teen avoid gang involvement?','["Carrying a weapon", "Joining a gang for protection", "Joining positive activities and staying connected with supportive adults", "Skipping school"]'::jsonb,2,'Positive connections reduce risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.10.A',3,'A common tactic used by human traffickers is to do what?','["Pay full wages", "Offer free tickets honestly", "Announce their plans", "Offer false promises of jobs or relationships to gain trust"]'::jsonb,3,'Traffickers use deception.','original'),
('115.38.c.10.B',3,'Gang recruitment often targets teens by doing what?','["Offering a sense of belonging, status or protection", "Offering safe schools", "Offering scholarships", "Offering careers"]'::jsonb,0,'Recruiters exploit needs for belonging.','original'),
('115.38.c.10.B',3,'One risk of gang involvement is what?','["Better safety", "Higher exposure to violence and legal trouble", "More freedom", "Guaranteed jobs"]'::jsonb,1,'Gangs expose members to harm.','original'),
('115.38.c.11.A',3,'A stranger online asks a teen to keep their chat a secret and to send a photo. The teen should do what?','["Keep it secret", "Share their address", "Refuse, stop talking and tell a trusted adult", "Send the photo"]'::jsonb,2,'Secrecy and photo requests are warning signs.','original'),
('115.38.c.11.A',3,'Which online habit best protects privacy?','["Sharing passwords", "Posting your address", "Accepting all requests", "Setting accounts to private and not sharing location"]'::jsonb,3,'Privacy settings reduce risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.11.B',3,'If someone sends a threatening message online, a teen should do what?','["Save the evidence, not respond, and report it to a trusted adult", "Reply with threats", "Delete everything", "Ignore forever"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence helps adults respond.','original'),
('115.38.c.11.B',3,'Sexting is risky for teens because shared images can do what?','["Be deleted forever", "Spread beyond the sender''s control and may have legal consequences", "Stay private always", "Cause no harm"]'::jsonb,1,'Images can be copied and shared.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.A',3,'Exposure to family violence can lead to cyclical patterns because children may do what?','["Never be affected", "Become immune", "Learn violent behavior as normal and repeat it unless they get help", "Always avoid conflict"]'::jsonb,2,'Cycles can be broken with support.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.A',3,'Which step can help break a cycle of family violence?','["Ignoring it", "Retaliating", "Hiding it", "Seeking counseling and support from trusted adults"]'::jsonb,3,'Support and counseling help.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.B',3,'A personal action plan for bullying should include what?','["People to tell, places to go for help and how to respond", "Revenge steps", "Staying home forever", "Silence"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans identify supports.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.B',3,'A student who sees bullying can help by doing what?','["Filming it for fun", "Supporting the target and reporting it to an adult", "Ignoring it", "Joining in"]'::jsonb,1,'Bystanders can help safely.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.C',3,'A possible legal consequence of bullying can be what?','["Extra recess", "Nothing ever", "Suspension or criminal charges depending on the behavior", "A prize"]'::jsonb,2,'Serious bullying can bring legal penalties.','original'),
('115.38.c.12.C',3,'Bullying can harm the person who bullies because it may lead to what?','["More friends", "Higher trust", "A better record", "Discipline and damaged relationships"]'::jsonb,3,'There are consequences for everyone.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.A',2,'A drug label that lists "antihistamine" tells you the drug belongs to which category?','["Allergy medication", "Vitamin", "Antibiotic", "Pain reliever"]'::jsonb,0,'Labels identify drug categories and uses.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.A',2,'On an over-the-counter label, "Directions" tell you what?','["The price", "How much to take and how often", "Where it was shipped", "The color"]'::jsonb,1,'Follow label directions.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.B',3,'Which is the safest way to store prescription medicine at home?','["In a backpack", "Shared with friends", "In a locked cabinet away from children and visitors", "On a counter"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe storage prevents misuse.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.B',3,'Unused prescription pills should be disposed of by doing what?','["Flushing at random", "Saving for later", "Sharing them", "Using a drug take-back site or program"]'::jsonb,3,'Take-back programs are safest.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.C',3,'Misusing a prescription drug includes what?','["Taking a drug prescribed for someone else", "Following the label", "Asking a doctor", "Taking as prescribed"]'::jsonb,0,'Only the prescribed person should take it.','original'),
('115.38.c.13.C',3,'A warning sign of prescription drug misuse is what?','["Following directions", "Taking more than directed or taking it to get high", "Finishing a course", "Asking a pharmacist"]'::jsonb,1,'Misuse deviates from directions.','original'),
('115.38.c.15.A',3,'Treatment options for substance use disorder can include what?','["Punishment only", "Hiding it", "Counseling, medication-assisted treatment and support groups", "Ignoring it"]'::jsonb,2,'Treatment is available.','original'),
('115.38.c.15.A',3,'Addiction is best described as what?','["A lack of willpower only", "Harmless", "A choice with no help", "A chronic health condition that affects the brain"]'::jsonb,3,'Addiction is treatable.','original'),
('115.38.c.15.B',3,'A teen who suspects a friend is abusing drugs should do what?','["Tell a parent, teacher or counselor", "Post about it", "Join in", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,0,'Trusted adults can get help.','original'),
('115.38.c.15.B',3,'Reporting suspected drug abuse to a trusted adult shows what?','["Disloyalty", "Care for the person''s safety", "Gossip", "Weakness"]'::jsonb,1,'It can save a life.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.A',3,'A physical influence on substance use is what?','["Positive friends", "Being active", "Easy access to the substance at home", "Supportive adults"]'::jsonb,2,'Availability increases risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.A',3,'A social influence on substance use is what?','["Sleeping well", "Studying", "Joining a club", "Peer pressure to try alcohol at a party"]'::jsonb,3,'Peers influence behavior.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.B',3,'A student organizes a school campaign for a substance-free life. This is an example of what?','["Health advocacy", "Avoidance", "Isolation", "Peer pressure"]'::jsonb,0,'Advocacy promotes health.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.B',3,'A good health advocacy message is one that is what?','["Hidden", "Accurate, clear and aimed at a specific audience", "Misleading", "Vague"]'::jsonb,1,'Messages must be accurate.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.C',3,'Which is a school-related effort to address health-risk behaviors?','["Secret meetings", "Ignoring them", "Peer-led programs and awareness weeks", "Banning all talk"]'::jsonb,2,'Schools can organize prevention.','original'),
('115.38.c.16.C',3,'A teen can participate in school health efforts by doing what?','["Hiding", "Spreading rumors", "Skipping events", "Volunteering for a peer education team"]'::jsonb,3,'Participation helps the community.','original'),
('115.38.c.17.A',3,'A refusal skill for saying no to alcohol is what?','["Saying no clearly, suggesting an alternative and leaving", "Making excuses and staying", "Laughing it off", "Saying maybe"]'::jsonb,0,'Refusal skills lower risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.17.A',3,'Using refusal skills helps teens avoid substances because they do what?','["Remove choices", "Give a plan to resist pressure", "Increase pressure", "Increase risk"]'::jsonb,1,'A plan makes saying no easier.','original'),
('115.38.c.17.B',3,'Alcohol and other drugs increase the risk of unsafe situations such as sexual assault because they do what?','["Prevent all harm", "Improve judgment", "Impair judgment and the ability to give or withdraw consent", "Make people safer"]'::jsonb,2,'Impairment affects safety and consent.','original'),
('115.38.c.17.B',3,'If a person cannot think clearly because of alcohol or drugs, they are able to give consent. True or false?','["True", "True only at parties", "True with a friend", "False; consent requires a clear, voluntary yes"]'::jsonb,3,'Impaired people cannot consent.','original'),
('115.38.c.18.A',3,'Healthy friendships provide a foundation for healthy dating relationships by building what?','["Trust, respect and communication", "Jealousy", "Control", "Secrecy"]'::jsonb,0,'Friendship skills carry over.','original'),
('115.38.c.18.A',3,'Which is a quality of a healthy friendship?','["Pressure", "Mutual respect and honesty", "Isolation", "Control"]'::jsonb,1,'Healthy relationships are equal.','original'),
('115.38.c.18.B',3,'Which character trait promotes a healthy dating relationship?','["Pressure", "Jealous control", "Respect for the other person''s boundaries", "Dishonesty"]'::jsonb,2,'Respect is essential.','original'),
('115.38.c.18.B',3,'Commitment and honest communication are important in marriage because they do what?','["Avoid problems", "Create secrecy", "Prevent talking", "Build trust over time"]'::jsonb,3,'Strong relationships need both.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
