('115.38.c.18.C',3,'A healthy marriage can support children by doing what?','["Providing a stable, supportive environment", "Limiting support", "Isolating them", "Creating instability"]'::jsonb,0,'Stability helps children.','original'),
('115.38.c.18.C',3,'Which factor in a family helps children develop well?','["Neglect", "Consistent care, love and communication", "Unpredictability", "Conflict only"]'::jsonb,1,'Nurturing homes support growth.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.A',3,'Grooming in sex trafficking involves what?','["Giving honest advice", "Offering a fair job", "Building trust with a person to later exploit them", "Teaching a skill"]'::jsonb,2,'Traffickers manipulate trust.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.A',3,'Which is a sign of coercion?','["A fair agreement", "Free choice", "Respect", "Threats or pressure to make someone do something against their will"]'::jsonb,3,'Coercion removes choice.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.B',3,'A characteristic of a harmful dating relationship is what?','["A partner who tries to control who you see and what you do", "Respecting your time", "Honest talks", "Supporting friends"]'::jsonb,0,'Control can lead to violence.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.B',3,'Constant jealousy, name-calling and checking your phone may be signs of what?','["Trust", "An unhealthy relationship that can lead to dating violence", "Respect", "Healthy love"]'::jsonb,1,'These are warning signs.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.C',3,'A strategy for preventing abuse is what?','["Ignoring discomfort", "Keeping secrets", "Knowing safe adults and trusting your instincts when something feels wrong", "Staying silent"]'::jsonb,2,'Awareness and support protect.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.C',3,'If an adult touches a teen in a way that feels wrong, the teen should do what?','["Keep it secret", "Stay quiet", "Blame themselves", "Say no, get away and tell a trusted adult"]'::jsonb,3,'Abuse is never the victim''s fault.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.D',3,'Making and respecting decisions about personal boundaries means what?','["Setting limits for yourself and honoring the limits of others", "Ignoring limits", "Pressuring others", "Having no limits"]'::jsonb,0,'Boundaries protect everyone.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.D',3,'A healthy sense of self helps a teen make safer choices because it does what?','["Encourages pressure", "Builds confidence to set limits", "Reduces confidence", "Increases doubt"]'::jsonb,1,'Self-worth supports boundaries.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.E',3,'Saying "No, I''m not comfortable with that" and walking away is an example of what?','["An aggressive reaction", "A passive response", "An assertive refusal strategy", "Giving in"]'::jsonb,2,'Assertive refusals are clear and calm.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.E',3,'A good refusal strategy for unhealthy behavior is to do what?','["Apologize and agree", "Stay quiet", "Hesitate", "Say no firmly, give a reason or alternative and leave if needed"]'::jsonb,3,'Be clear and direct.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.F',3,'Alcohol and other substances increase sexual risk because they do what?','["Impair judgment and make unsafe choices more likely", "Prevent risk", "Improve judgment", "Increase safety"]'::jsonb,0,'Impairment raises risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.F',3,'Setting limits before a date helps because it does what?','["Creates confusion", "Gives you a plan so you are less pressured in the moment", "Increases pressure", "Avoids all dating"]'::jsonb,1,'Plans support decisions.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.G',3,'It is wrong to violate another person''s boundaries because everyone has the right to what?','["Ignore others", "Control others", "Decide what happens to their own body", "Pressure others"]'::jsonb,2,'Consent matters.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.G',3,'Pressure to become sexually active can come from what?','["Only teachers", "Nowhere", "Only parents", "Peers, media or a partner"]'::jsonb,3,'Pressure has many sources.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.H',3,'A teen who experiences sexual harassment should do what?','["Report it to a parent or other trusted adult", "Keep it secret", "Ignore it", "Retaliate"]'::jsonb,0,'Reporting is important.','original'),
('115.38.c.19.H',3,'Reporting sexual abuse is important because it can do what?','["Create blame", "Protect the victim and others from further harm", "Delay help", "Cause trouble"]'::jsonb,1,'Reporting leads to help.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.A',3,'One impact of teen pregnancy on a young parent is what?','["Free tuition", "No costs", "Greater financial and educational challenges", "Less responsibility"]'::jsonb,2,'Parenting affects education and finances.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.A',3,'Raising a child requires large costs such as what?','["Free daycare", "Free housing", "No expenses", "Health care, childcare and housing"]'::jsonb,3,'Costs add up.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.B',3,'STDs/STIs can be transmitted through what?','["Sexual contact, and some through blood or from mother to baby", "Shaking hands", "Hugging", "Sharing a desk"]'::jsonb,0,'Modes vary by infection.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.B',3,'Which is NOT a way STIs are spread?','["Mother to baby", "Using the same classroom", "Contaminated needles", "Sexual contact"]'::jsonb,1,'Casual contact does not spread STIs.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.C',3,'Statistics from the CDC show that STI rates among young people are what?','["Zero", "Not tracked", "Higher than among older adults", "Lower than adults"]'::jsonb,2,'Young people have high rates.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.C',3,'A reliable source for STI statistics is what?','["A rumor", "A random site", "A friend", "The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention"]'::jsonb,3,'Use credible sources.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.D',3,'Some STIs, such as HPV and chlamydia, can have what?','["No symptoms at all, so testing is important", "Obvious signs", "Always visible signs", "Immediate pain"]'::jsonb,0,'Many infections are silent.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.D',3,'HIV attacks the body''s what?','["Hair", "Immune system", "Skin", "Bones"]'::jsonb,1,'HIV weakens immunity.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.E',3,'Early testing for STIs matters because it does what?','["Delays care", "Is not helpful", "Allows early treatment and prevents spread", "Causes infection"]'::jsonb,2,'Early treatment is effective.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.E',3,'A sexually active person should be screened for STIs how often?','["Never", "Only if sick", "Once as a child", "As recommended by a health care provider"]'::jsonb,3,'Screening depends on risk.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.F',3,'Emotional risks of sexual activity for school-age teens can include what?','["Stress, anxiety and depression", "Guaranteed happiness", "No feelings", "Less worry"]'::jsonb,0,'Emotions matter.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.F',3,'Why might a teen feel regret after becoming sexually active too early?','["It is always positive", "They may not be emotionally ready for the consequences", "It is simple", "It is risk-free"]'::jsonb,1,'Readiness matters.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.G',3,'Abstinence from sexual activity is the only method that is what?','["Unreliable", "Partly effective", "100 percent effective at preventing pregnancy and STIs", "Not effective"]'::jsonb,2,'Abstinence eliminates the risk.','original'),
