('115.38.c.21.H',3,'A teen can build support for abstinence by doing what?','["Talking with parents and surrounding themselves with supportive peers", "Hiding choices", "Ignoring advice", "Isolating"]'::jsonb,0,'Support helps.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.H',3,'Peer support for healthy choices can be built by doing what?','["Following pressure", "Joining groups that share the same values", "Avoiding people", "Hiding"]'::jsonb,1,'Peers help.','original'),
('115.38.c.21.I',3,'Contraceptive failure rates in typical use are often higher than in perfect use because of what?','["Rare mistakes", "Random luck", "Human error, such as inconsistent or incorrect use", "Perfect behavior"]'::jsonb,2,'Typical use includes mistakes.','original'),
